<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lai Ching-te</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1959">1959</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as William Lai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lai Ching-te is a Taiwanese politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-progressive-party">Democratic Progressive Party</a>, a former physician who served as mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tainan">Tainan</a>, premier and vice-president. He won the presidential election of January 2024 and took office as president of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in May 2024, the first time a party had won three consecutive presidential terms since direct elections began.</p></div>
